# Mechanics 02 — Block on a rough incline, pulled by a hanging mass
#
# (Halliday/Resnick ch. 5–6 and 10; Kleppner & Kolenkow ch. 2.)
# A block m₁ = 4.00 kg sits on a 30.0° incline. A string runs from it, up the
# slope, over a pulley (a uniform disk, M = 1.00 kg, R = 10.0 cm, the string
# does not slip) to a hanging mass m₂ = 3.50 kg. The system starts from rest.
#
#   (a) With kinetic friction μ_k = 0.150: the acceleration and the two string
#       tensions (on the incline side and on the hanging side).
#   (b) The minimum static friction coefficient that would keep the system at rest.
#   (c) Now the slope gets rougher as the block climbs: μ(x) = μ₀ + β x with
#       μ₀ = 0.150 and β = 0.400 per metre. Using the work–energy theorem, find
#       the speed after 0.50 m, the largest speed, and where the block stops.
#   (d) Solve the equation of motion and check (c); the time to stop is half a
#       period of a harmonic oscillator.

m1 = 4.00 kg
m2 = 3.50 kg
θ = 30.0°
M_pulley = 1.00 kg
R = 10.0 cm
μ_k = 0.150
g = 9.81 m/s²

I = ½ M_pulley R²
M_eff = m1 + m2 + I / R²            # everything moves with the string

# (a) constant friction
F_net = m2 g - m1 g sin(θ) - μ_k m1 g cos(θ)
a = F_net / M_eff
T1 = m1 a + m1 g sin(θ) + μ_k m1 g cos(θ)     # incline side
T2 = m2 g - m2 a                              # hanging side
print "acceleration:", a to 6 digits
print "tension, incline side:", T1 to 6 digits
print "tension, hanging side:", T2 to 6 digits
print "torque check (T2 - T1) R = I a/R:", (T2 - T1) R ~= I a / R

# (b) static friction needed to hold it
μ_s_min = (m2 - m1 sin(θ)) / (m1 cos(θ))
print "minimum static coefficient:", μ_s_min to 6 digits

# (c) position-dependent friction: work-energy theorem
μ0 = 0.150
β = 0.400 /m
F(x) = m2 g - m1 g sin(θ) - (μ0 + β x) m1 g cos(θ)
W(s) = ∫ F(x) dx from 0 m to s
speed(s) = √(2 W(s) / M_eff)
print "speed after 0.50 m:", speed(0.50 m) to 6 digits

c_spring = β m1 g cos(θ)            # F(x) = F(0) - c x: a spring-like force
x_vmax = F(0 m) / c_spring
x_stop = 2 x_vmax
print "largest speed:", speed(x_vmax) to 6 digits, "at", x_vmax to 6 digits
print "stops after:", x_stop to 6 digits
print "work done at the stop (should be 0):", W(x_stop)
solve W(s_stop) = 0 J for s_stop from 1 cm to 10 m       # the same stop, found numerically
print "stop from W(s) = 0:", s_stop in m to 6 digits

# (d) equation of motion
t_half = π √(M_eff / c_spring)
solve x'' = F(x) / M_eff
  with x(0) = 0 m, x'(0) = 0 m/s
  for t from 0 s to t_half
print "time to stop:", t_half to 6 digits
print "ODE position at that time:", x(t_half) to 6 digits
# The speed at a given position: first find when x = 0.50 m
solve x(t_05) = 0.50 m for t_05 from 0 s to t_half
print "ODE speed after 0.50 m:", x'(t_05) to 6 digits
